<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38839" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπήρεια</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί, ἄρος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>insulting treatment, abuse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθροῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				4.5
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὸν χορόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελεύειν κατ᾽ ἐπήρειαν</span>
			order <i>haughtily</i> or <i>by way of insult,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἐ. τινος γεγένηταί
			τι</span> is done to <i>insult</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				Amips.
				9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἐπήρειαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					180.8
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθόνον τ᾽ ἐ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					92.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἐπηρείας τάξει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ πρὸς ἐπήρειαν καὶ χάριν
					πράττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1287a38
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἐ. τὴν ἐμήν</span> ib.
				<i><span class="en">
				195.20
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρὶς ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					262.24
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				4.331
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃστρικαὶ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chor.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rev.Phil.</u>
				1.73
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. δαίμονός τινος</span> his
				<i>capricious dealing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Laps.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				18
			</span></i>:—later spelt <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπήρια</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				340.21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Melamp.
			</span></i>(?) in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRyl.</u>
				28.139
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>.</div>
